      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 5.53,
          "en": "Now to get started with the Bare Workflow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.53,
          "end": 9.19,
          "en": "it's best if you simply search for Expo Bare Workflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.19,
          "end": 11.72,
          "en": "and you should find a Getting Started page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.72,
          "end": 14.593,
          "en": "well, that gets you started with that Workflow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.56,
          "end": 18.66,
          "en": "Now here you'll learn how you can create a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.66,
          "end": 22.62,
          "en": "that uses this Expo Workflow this Bare Workflow now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.62,
          "end": 25.1,
          "en": "and there is one note I wanna make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.1,
          "end": 29.16,
          "en": "before you try going through these steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.16,
          "end": 31.13,
          "en": "When we used the Manage Workflow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.13,
          "end": 34.75,
          "en": "as mentioned before we used the Expo Go app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.75,
          "end": 37.193,
          "en": "for previewing our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.64,
          "end": 39.97,
          "en": "With the Bare Workflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.97,
          "end": 44.37,
          "en": "you can also use this Expo Go app for easy previews",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.37,
          "end": 47.14,
          "en": "but there are restrictions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.14,
          "end": 50.87,
          "en": "When you use Expo Go and you also have an app that uses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.87,
          "end": 53.47,
          "en": "native device code written by you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.47,
          "end": 56.35,
          "en": "the Expo Go app won't support that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.35,
          "end": 59.96,
          "en": "because it can't load and execute that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.96,
          "end": 64.32,
          "en": "Therefore often when using this Bare Workflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.32,
          "end": 67.47,
          "en": "you will not be able or you might not be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.47,
          "end": 69.31,
          "en": "to use the Expo Go app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.31,
          "end": 71.52,
          "en": "And therefore, what you need to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 74.5,
          "en": "is you need to set up your local machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.5,
          "end": 78.51,
          "en": "your computer, such that iOS or Android apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.51,
          "end": 81.03999999999999,
          "en": "can be built on your local machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.03999999999999,
          "end": 82.9,
          "en": "because they need to be built there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.9,
          "end": 84.44,
          "en": "because they will then be built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.44,
          "end": 87.77,
          "en": "before they are shipped to the emulators for preview.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.77,
          "end": 90.52,
          "en": "So you have to build an app standalone apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.52,
          "end": 93.34,
          "en": "on your machine first, before you can preview them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.34,
          "end": 96.97,
          "en": "because you can't use this Expo Go wrapper app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.97,
          "end": 99.95,
          "en": "And for this reason my recommendation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.95,
          "end": 102.413,
          "en": "is that you go to reactnative.dev",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.85499999999999,
          "end": 108.25,
          "en": "and there, I recommend that you do go to environment set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.25,
          "end": 110.27199999999999,
          "en": "and you set up your development environment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.27199999999999,
          "end": 113.112,
          "en": "for local development without Expo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.112,
          "end": 115.672,
          "en": "because you will need the same environment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.672,
          "end": 117.36099999999999,
          "en": "if you use the React Native CLI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.36099999999999,
          "end": 121.528,
          "en": "or the Expo Bare Workflow without the Expo Go app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.512,
          "end": 124.61,
          "en": "So under setting up the development environment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.61,
          "end": 127.56,
          "en": "you wanna go to the React Native CLI Quickstart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.56,
          "end": 129.71,
          "en": "and then follow the different steps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.71,
          "end": 131.7,
          "en": "for your operating system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.7,
          "end": 134.43,
          "en": "and the platform you wanna build for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.43,
          "end": 137.06,
          "en": "However, here's one important restriction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.06,
          "end": 141.21,
          "en": "You can only build iOS apps if you have a macOS system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.21,
          "end": 144.35,
          "en": "So on macOS you can build Android and iOS apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.35,
          "end": 147.82,
          "en": "on Windows and Linux iOS apps are not supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.82,
          "end": 149.87,
          "en": "You can't build and preview them there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.87,
          "end": 151.68,
          "en": "That's one important difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.68,
          "end": 155.363,
          "en": "compared to the Managed Workflow that embraced Expo Go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.39,
          "end": 159.48,
          "en": "You can build Android apps on Windows and Linux though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.48,
          "end": 162.42000000000002,
          "en": "and therefore you can of course still do at least that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.42000000000002,
          "end": 165.52,
          "en": "on your local machine when using the Bare Workflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.52,
          "end": 167.213,
          "en": "or the React Native CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.21,
          "end": 171.1,
          "en": "So definitely go through these set up steps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.1,
          "end": 173.7,
          "en": "which you find here for your operating system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.7,
          "end": 176.56,
          "en": "so that you are able to use the Bare Workflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.56,
          "end": 178.32999999999998,
          "en": "without the Expo Go app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.32999999999998,
          "end": 181.76,
